---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// REWRITTEN 2026-07-31 for scannability, not length. The page already said all
// of this, in twelve paragraphs averaging 55 words, nine of which ran over 40.
// Over 40 words is roughly where a reader skips the block entirely. Nothing
// true was cut: prose became lists, figures became figures, and the Coldwell
// Banker example became a list of what we actually produce rather than a
// paragraph describing it.
---
<Layout
  title="About | SDub Media Nashville Video Production"
  description="A five-person video and photo team in Nolensville, working across Nashville. Recurring content for businesses, corporate events, dance, listings and a few weddings a year."
>
<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>One team, one system,<br>same quality every week</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">Businesses need to show up on video consistently, not once. We build the system that makes that happen.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-num">5</span><span class="stat-label">People, covering video, photography and editing</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-num">19</span><span class="stat-label">Pieces of content from a single interview day</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat-num">6</span><span class="stat-label">Coldwell Banker offices we shoot across</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why recurring</span>
    <h2>One video won't move your business. Fifty will.</h2>
    <p>Most companies treat video as an event. They save up, book a big shoot, post it once, then go quiet for six months.</p>
    <p>Showing up is a habit, not a moment. The hard part was never the camera. It was the consistency.</p>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><strong>Planning</strong> built around your calendar, not ours</li>
      <li><strong>Batched shoots</strong>, so the work stays efficient</li>
      <li><strong>One consistent style</strong>, so every piece looks like one brand</li>
      <li><strong>Editing in house</strong>, so the pipeline does not stall when things get busy</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">The model in action</span>
    <h2>What that looks like in practice</h2>
    <p>Coldwell Banker Southern Realty has eight offices across Tennessee. We have shot at six of them, and the relationship runs in several formats at once.</p>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li>A <strong>weekly series</strong> filmed with the owner at the main Nashville office</li>
      <li><strong>Monthly headshot days</strong>, rotating through the offices one at a time</li>
      <li>Recurring content produced in their <strong>in-house podcast room</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Live events</strong>, where they bring in speakers to address every office</li>
      <li>Work for their luxury division, <strong>Coldwell Banker Global Luxury</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">We work directly with their director of marketing, so the video runs as part of their plan rather than arriving as separate bookings. We are not handed a shot list, and they are not left running a production department.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Range</span>
    <h2>The work we take on</h2>
    <p>Five kinds of work, all the same shape. You get the complete record, and the short piece you can actually use.</p>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><a href="/business"><strong>Businesses</strong></a>: one sitting, cut into a quarter of content</li>
      <li><a href="/corporate-events"><strong>Conferences</strong></a>: every main-stage talk archived, plus a highlight reel</li>
      <li><a href="/dance"><strong>Dance studios</strong></a>: the full recital for families, a short cut for the website</li>
      <li><a href="/real-estate-photography"><strong>Listings</strong></a>: a full gallery back in 48 hours, priced per listing</li>
      <li><a href="/weddings"><strong>Weddings</strong></a>: a full film and a sizzle reel</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Coldwell Banker Southern Realty, Global Luxury and the Middle of the Story Podcast are weekly. Webb School and Nolensville Dance Company come back once or twice a year, which is its own kind of trust.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Weddings</span>
    <h2>And a few weddings a year</h2>
    <p>Fewer than we used to take, by choice. Most of the week goes to business clients now, which is exactly why the weddings we book are unhurried. Nobody's film gets edited between three other jobs.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="background: var(--soft);">
  <div class="container-narrow text-center">
    <span class="eyebrow">Where we are</span>
    <h2>Rooted in Nolensville, working across Nashville</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem;">Twenty minutes south of downtown. Most of the work is in the city, and some of our favourite clients are right here at home.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a conversation</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
